{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 173, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 173, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=174&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=172&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 171280147, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r171280147-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Large Hindu Temple which needs cleaning and more care", "text": "This is a very large Hindu temple and unless you are a Hindu, you would not be allowed to go into the temple. For Europeans, there is a fee of Rs. 1,000 per person and if you are from a SAARC country, you will be allowed to go in free of charge. Although the temple is out of bounds for Non-Hindus the rest of the premises houses a lot of things that might be of interest to you. This place has a lot of examples from classical Hindu architecture and there is a bit of a climb to get to the top of this place as well. You will have to cross a bridge and the view here is extremely beautiful although the river itself is not that clean. However, you will not be able to enjoy much of that beauty because of the sellers who try to get your attention and practically stalk you!!!!\n\nWhen you get to the top, you would be able to find a quiet corner and enjoy a bit of peace in the midst of small shrines which are scattered all over the place. If you go up here, you might want to be careful of the bulls and the monkeys.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2013-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "A4041DA5DEFE6EC51D322AEFB2F226A3", "name": "mrsdanushkajayatunge", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/mrsdanushkajayatunge", "username": "mrsdanushkajayatunge", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e5/2b/default-avatar-2020-52.jpg", "contribution_count": 100, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 60890, "location_name": "Cambridge", "location_name_detailed": "Cambridge, Massachusetts"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-08-08", "published_at_date": "2013-08-07"}, {"review_id": 171132670, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r171132670-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Great but still need some cleaning at river side", "text": "It has a lot improvements there since last time, last time when i went there it wasnt maintained well but this time it was really appreciatable, and yes be careful of monkeys too", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2013-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "5EDEE28793DF80F9C8AA3E425A4428FB", "name": "Rob S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/265RobS", "username": "265RobS", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f1/b8/default-avatar-2020-22.jpg", "contribution_count": 72, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255100, "location_name": "Melbourne", "location_name_detailed": "Melbourne, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-08-07", "published_at_date": "2013-08-06"}, {"review_id": 171059158, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r171059158-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Pricey but worth it", "text": "This was expensive in relative terms and you are hassled at the gate to take on a guide. If we had more time, I would have negotiated one, but we only had an hour or so. Was interesting but beware of all the hawkers!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2013-07-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "6335F38AA299C0628B1E9DC26658EFB5", "name": "SnooPowell", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/SnooPowell", "username": "SnooPowell", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f4/5d/default-avatar-2020-32.jpg", "contribution_count": 55, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 635924, "location_name": "Godalming", "location_name_detailed": "Godalming, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-08-06", "published_at_date": "2013-08-06"}, {"review_id": 170794900, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r170794900-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Religious importance", "text": "Pashupatinath temple is one of the holiest temples in the Hindu religion. Flocks of devotees throng the temple and it is said sins are absolved after a visit. The pujas thaat are conducted here are full of rituals. The temple is adjacent to a river but it has not much scenic beauty.Further only hindus are allowed into the premises.\nIt is a must  however for hindus  visiting Nepal.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 41, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2012-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "448D4F4E87F5426CAD4AC8206F0869DA", "name": "Ruchira K", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/ruchirak_13", "username": "ruchirak_13", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e2/11/default-avatar-2020-41.jpg", "contribution_count": 11, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-08-05", "published_at_date": "2013-08-04"}, {"review_id": 170534944, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r170534944-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Cultural shock", "text": "When you are have different culture and beliefs this place is a bit shock. Our guide well explained the place and crematorium area, I feel lucky that I don't have to see that. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2013-05-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "DF5541F60347A4E5BC45206ABA5C5A7B", "name": "Katharina R", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/katharinar2013", "username": "katharinar2013", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/04/4d/cd/1d/katharina-r.jpg", "contribution_count": 2, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-08-03", "published_at_date": "2013-08-03"}, {"review_id": 170382323, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r170382323-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Great hindu temple in the world", "text": "Pashupatinath is one of the biggest Hindus temple in the world.  The supreme holiness of the site stems from the Shiva linga enshrined in its main temple. It expresses the very essence of Hinduism as pilgrims, priests, devotes, temples, ashrams, images, inscriptions and cremation ghats intermingle with the rituals of daily life, all sprawled along the banks of the sacred Bagmati River. The temple’s origins are obscure.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 8, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2013-07-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "1CF24FD0AE6068CB6E08969E731BEE92", "name": "Saajan S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/prakashdahal", "username": "prakashdahal", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/02/35/fc/d4/prakashdahal.jpg", "contribution_count": 52, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-08-02", "published_at_date": "2013-08-01"}, {"review_id": 170382282, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r170382282-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Great hindu temple in the world", "text": "Pashupatinath is one of the biggest Hindus temple in the world. The supreme holiness of the site stems from the Shiva linga enshrined in its main temple. It expresses the very essence of Hinduism as pilgrims, priests, devotes, temples, ashrams, images, inscriptions and cremation ghats intermingle with the rituals of daily life, all sprawled along the banks of the sacred Bagmati River. The temple’s origins are obscure.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 7, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2013-07-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "1CF24FD0AE6068CB6E08969E731BEE92", "name": "Saajan S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/prakashdahal", "username": "prakashdahal", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/02/35/fc/d4/prakashdahal.jpg", "contribution_count": 52, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-08-02", "published_at_date": "2013-08-01"}, {"review_id": 170154688, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r170154688-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Do i belong here?", "text": "Pay round ten euro. U allowed to watch from the other side. Not allowed to cross the bridge to the temple. Can be shocking burning people. I feel like outsider watching private things. But the feeling to experience this is very special. Be respectfull with taking pictures.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2013-07-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "6F17848FF619D64CF2308F15453E90FD", "name": "Saskia K", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/saskia_keizer", "username": "saskia_keizer", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/06/18/60/72/saskia-keizer.jpg", "contribution_count": 188, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 227927, "location_name": "Hellendoorn", "location_name_detailed": "Hellendoorn, The Netherlands"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-07-31", "published_at_date": "2013-07-31"}, {"review_id": 169840854, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r169840854-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "strong place", "text": "very strong and magic experience, must see place in Kathmandu.everytime i am comming back to see ,,little varanasi,,if you have more time, you can spend more time in this place and visit forest and places without any tourists.", "review_tip": nu